  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The political environment in Indonesia has shifted following a Supreme Court ruling regarding the educational credentials of Vice President Gibran. Following the ruling, the Vice President held discussions with President Prabowo, during which he expressed an intention to resign from his position. According to reports, the President advised him to remain in office and contest the court's decision through legal channels. Various political stakeholders, including members of the PKS and Golkar parties, have since weighed in on the situation, emphasizing the importance of constitutional procedures for resignation, which involve the House of Representatives. Legal experts have also outlined the formal process for filling a vacancy in the vice presidency should the position become vacant. As of now, the situation remains a focus of ongoing deliberation between the executive branch and legislative representatives regarding the procedural requirements and the future of the current vice presidential tenure.",
